---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DownloadCta from '../components/DownloadCta.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Download Grafyn"
  description="Install Grafyn on Windows, macOS, or Linux. Point it at a markdown folder."
>
  <article class="px-4 pt-32 pb-24 md:px-10 md:pt-40 lg:px-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-paper md:text-4xl">
        Download Grafyn
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[40ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-mute">
        One installer per platform. Auto-updates after install — the app checks
        GitHub for new releases. The button below follows your OS.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10">
        <DownloadCta compact />
      </div>

      <section class="mt-20 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-paper md:text-2xl">First run</h2>
        <ol class="mt-6 space-y-6 text-mute">
          <li>
            <p class="font-medium text-paper">Vault path</p>
            <p class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              Where your markdown lives. Default is <code class="font-mono text-sm text-paper">~/Documents/Grafyn/vault/</code>. Point it at an existing folder and Grafyn indexes it.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="font-medium text-paper">Model runtime (optional)</p>
            <p class="mt-1 leading-relaxed">
              An OpenRouter key (a hosted model API) powers the canvas,
              distillation, and twin answers. Skip it if you only want the
              vault, or run models locally with Ollama instead.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-paper md:text-2xl">Platforms</h2>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-mute">
          <li>Windows x64 and ARM64</li>
          <li>macOS Apple Silicon</li>
          <li>Linux .deb and AppImage</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 text-mute">
          Alongside the app, the installer adds a small local MCP server so
          tools like Claude Desktop can read and write your vault. It only
          runs while Grafyn runs.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
